1
00:00:05,400 --> 00:00:06,401
[This drama is intended for entertainment purposes only.]

2
00:00:06,411 --> 00:00:08,400
[All characters, behaviors, locations, and events depicted are fictional.]

3
00:00:08,430 --> 00:00:09,950
[It is not intended to be sexually suggestive or to encourage viewers]

4
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:11,501
[to engage in inappropriate or morally objectionable behavior.]

5
00:00:11,511 --> 00:00:12,890
[Nor is it intended to discredit any profession]

6
00:00:12,899 --> 00:00:13,900
[or create negative perceptions of any organization]

7
00:00:13,911 --> 00:00:14,912
[or any particular group of people.]

8
00:00:15,070 --> 00:00:17,800
Tell whoever hired you that you got the job done.

9
00:00:17,871 --> 00:00:19,040
I'll play along.

10
00:00:19,072 --> 00:00:20,547
You need to go to the police right now.

11
00:00:20,600 --> 00:00:22,520
About both what happened to you and your sister.

12
00:00:22,601 --> 00:00:24,320
Even if I report it, the police won't do a thing.

13
00:00:24,430 --> 00:00:26,360
The only way to lure a tiger out of its den

14
00:00:26,431 --> 00:00:27,720
is to provoke it until it gets angry

15
00:00:27,795 --> 00:00:29,360
and comes charging out so we can catch it.

16
00:00:29,438 --> 00:00:30,774
And how are you going to provoke her

17
00:00:31,039 --> 00:00:32,800
into sending someone after you again?

18
00:00:32,992 --> 00:00:35,200
I'll do exactly what Mutta did.

19
00:00:35,302 --> 00:00:37,880
Let's have some fun after the event, okay?

20
00:00:37,903 --> 00:00:39,960
After the event, we're going all out.

21
00:00:41,987 --> 00:00:45,040
Oh, I wasn't aware that the minister would be joining us.

22
00:00:45,112 --> 00:00:47,720
In that case, may I invite Minister Nopnapha

23
00:00:47,955 --> 00:00:50,500
to present the token of appreciation to Director Jenphop?

24
00:00:50,956 --> 00:00:53,360
Look at them posing together. A husband and his two wives!

25
00:00:53,907 --> 00:00:57,308
Honesty is one of our core values.

26
00:00:57,411 --> 00:00:59,700
We must never steal someone else's spouse.

27
00:00:59,886 --> 00:01:02,160
Looks like our plans for tonight are off, Director.

28
00:01:02,182 --> 00:01:03,400
I'll be going now.

29
00:01:05,451 --> 00:01:08,080
Mutta. So how about we have a civilized conversation?

30
00:01:08,112 --> 00:01:09,320
I'll count

31
00:01:09,531 --> 00:01:11,320
how many words we can exchange before things turn ugly.

32
00:01:11,332 --> 00:01:12,333
Mutta, you bitch!

33
00:01:26,741 --> 00:01:28,139
Hello. Have you got a table yet?

34
00:01:28,166 --> 00:01:29,167
Yes, I have.

35
00:01:44,560 --> 00:01:45,761
We finally get to see each other.

36
00:01:46,040 --> 00:01:48,680
I've only seen you on video calls. Your face looked so tiny.

37
00:01:48,774 --> 00:01:51,270
You're much bigger in person than you used to be.

38
00:01:52,075 --> 00:01:53,076
Oh, come on.

39
00:01:53,734 --> 00:01:55,440
Aren't we the same size?

40
00:01:56,523 --> 00:02:00,520
When we were kids, we could share all our clothes and shoes.

41
00:02:01,056 --> 00:02:03,500
Oh, by the way, I brought something back for you.

42
00:02:08,179 --> 00:02:09,180
What is it?

43
00:02:11,400 --> 00:02:12,840
Something I took from you.

44
00:02:26,798 --> 00:02:28,760
That was 20 years ago.

45
00:02:29,912 --> 00:02:31,064
You still haven't forgotten about it?

46
00:02:36,395 --> 00:02:40,250
I have dozens of pairs of designer shoes now.

47
00:02:41,611 --> 00:02:43,680
I'm not holding a grudge over something from our childhood anymore.

48
00:02:55,110 --> 00:02:58,400
I'm here to have dinner with my twin sister, whom I haven't seen in ages.

49
00:02:59,264 --> 00:03:01,560
We'll have steak and wine.

50
00:03:02,352 --> 00:03:05,280
Maybe we'll get some dessert afterward.

51
00:03:07,024 --> 00:03:08,025
Is it okay?

52
00:03:11,110 --> 00:03:14,680
It says the speaker is happy and relaxed.

53
00:03:14,731 --> 00:03:17,720
"Her voice sounds hopeful. It's a bright day for her."

54
00:03:18,432 --> 00:03:20,040
So, how accurate is it?

55
00:03:20,486 --> 00:03:22,120
It's an AI that analyzes people's voices.

56
00:03:22,246 --> 00:03:24,560
I'm working on getting it to detect lies.

57
00:03:26,550 --> 00:03:29,403
Your work is so cutting-edge.

58
00:03:30,224 --> 00:03:32,120
No wonder you make so much money.

59
00:03:32,550 --> 00:03:35,010
You can even afford to buy land in Khao Yai.

60
00:03:36,022 --> 00:03:38,023
But the stress is just as high.

61
00:03:38,390 --> 00:03:41,120
Oh, by the way, our house plans are ready.

62
00:03:41,195 --> 00:03:43,000
I had an architect friend design them for us.

63
00:03:52,043 --> 00:03:53,044
They're so cute.

64
00:03:54,843 --> 00:03:56,726
Just like the houses we used to draw as kids.

65
00:03:57,728 --> 00:04:00,240
I've already contacted a construction company, too.

66
00:04:00,576 --> 00:04:02,500
They can start laying the foundations next month.

67
00:04:02,720 --> 00:04:05,560
I told them to build both houses at the same time.

68
00:04:05,622 --> 00:04:07,958
Don't worry. I'll cover your share for now.

69
00:04:09,019 --> 00:04:10,928
Hey, you can't do that!

70
00:04:12,272 --> 00:04:13,880
Just go ahead and build yours first.

71
00:04:14,643 --> 00:04:16,120
I've almost saved up enough money.

72
00:04:16,800 --> 00:04:18,520
I can build mine later.

73
00:04:19,144 --> 00:04:22,718
I'm thinking of selling all my designer stuff.

74
00:04:23,598 --> 00:04:24,835
That should get me another...

75
00:04:25,726 --> 00:04:26,727
Million baht.

76
00:04:28,099 --> 00:04:30,920
I had no idea Thai civil servants were paid so well.

77
00:04:31,166 --> 00:04:33,250
No wonder you have so many luxury items.

78
00:04:35,622 --> 00:04:37,760
My government salary alone

79
00:04:38,265 --> 00:04:40,560
would barely cover this meal.

80
00:04:41,947 --> 00:04:44,050
But the reason I've managed to save up

81
00:04:47,211 --> 00:04:48,212
is that my boyfriend supports me financially.

82
00:04:50,304 --> 00:04:51,305
Your boyfriend?

83
00:04:51,805 --> 00:04:54,480
You have a boyfriend? You've never told me about him!

84
00:04:54,918 --> 00:04:55,919
Let me see.

85
00:04:56,312 --> 00:04:57,313
Show me a picture of him.

86
00:06:22,472 --> 00:06:25,662
Turn off the lights and CCTV cameras on the entire floor.

87
00:06:30,480 --> 00:06:32,678
With gold prices soaring past 70,000 baht per baht-weight,

88
00:06:34,496 --> 00:06:38,250
smart people make money trading stocks and Bitcoin.

89
00:06:39,347 --> 00:06:41,294
But a brainless woman like you

90
00:06:41,579 --> 00:06:44,250
still makes a living in the world's oldest profession.

91
00:06:45,998 --> 00:06:47,320
No investment required, right?

92
00:06:48,000 --> 00:06:50,401
You've had the tools of the trade since birth.

93
00:06:52,347 --> 00:06:53,450
All it takes is a little effort.

94
00:06:54,342 --> 00:06:56,960
Just a few pelvic muscle squeezes, and the job's done.

95
00:06:58,200 --> 00:06:59,601
You're absolutely pathetic.

96
00:07:00,856 --> 00:07:03,955
Because half the men in the world are still sick of their wives.

97
00:07:04,968 --> 00:07:06,702
And I happen to have certain qualities

98
00:07:08,000 --> 00:07:10,040
that an old wife like you just doesn't have.

99
00:07:10,726 --> 00:07:13,152
Why wouldn't I seize this market opportunity?

100
00:07:13,894 --> 00:07:15,200
The money's pretty good, too.

101
00:07:18,662 --> 00:07:19,663
You bitch, Mutta!

102
00:07:20,663 --> 00:07:21,764
Take that ring off right now!

103
00:07:27,211 --> 00:07:29,960
Your husband put it on my finger himself.

104
00:07:30,829 --> 00:07:31,900
Why don't you get him to take it off?

105
00:07:32,718 --> 00:07:34,720
Though he'd probably take all my clothes off, too.

106
00:07:35,374 --> 00:07:36,920
Because what he's got at home

107
00:07:38,300 --> 00:07:39,301
isn't exactly a pretty sight.

108
00:07:41,283 --> 00:07:42,400
Take it off right now!

109
00:07:49,320 --> 00:07:50,500
You bitch, Mutta!

110
00:07:57,806 --> 00:07:59,920
Remember this. From now on,

111
00:08:00,755 --> 00:08:02,200
you're Mutta's victim.

112
00:08:30,100 --> 00:08:32,000
Oh, that wasn't enough?

113
00:08:32,374 --> 00:08:33,375
Here's another one!

114
00:08:57,718 --> 00:08:59,800
Want some more? You got it!

115
00:09:11,440 --> 00:09:13,841
I'm sorry, but you can't leave just yet.

116
00:09:14,179 --> 00:09:15,795
Huh? Why not?

117
00:09:16,180 --> 00:09:17,440
Isn't the event over?

118
00:09:17,736 --> 00:09:19,177
Uh, Director?

119
00:09:19,326 --> 00:09:20,500
Director?

120
00:09:31,667 --> 00:09:33,560
Everyone, help!

121
00:09:33,683 --> 00:09:35,000
The Director fell down the stairs!

122
00:09:35,763 --> 00:09:36,764
Ma'am!

123
00:09:41,515 --> 00:09:42,516
Ma'am!

124
00:09:43,691 --> 00:09:44,692
Ma'am!

125
00:09:46,694 --> 00:09:47,695
- Oh!
- Oh my!

126
00:09:48,272 --> 00:09:49,273
Are you all right, ma'am?

127
00:09:50,900 --> 00:09:51,960
Where does it hurt?

128
00:09:53,100 --> 00:09:54,101
Aunt Nopnapha!

129
00:09:55,480 --> 00:09:56,700
- Easy now.
- Nopnapha!

130
00:09:56,723 --> 00:09:57,724
Try not to move too much.

131
00:10:09,195 --> 00:10:10,680
Don't film this! Stop filming!

132
00:10:10,715 --> 00:10:11,716
No filming!

133
00:10:16,200 --> 00:10:17,201
Uh...

134
00:10:17,774 --> 00:10:20,100
I'll ask the hotel to call the Poh Teck Tung Foundation.

135
00:10:21,510 --> 00:10:22,680
You mean an ambulance, Uncle?

136
00:10:24,400 --> 00:10:25,401
I'll leave it to you, Kit.

137
00:10:25,771 --> 00:10:26,800
Please excuse us.

138
00:10:27,000 --> 00:10:30,200
Be more careful next time, Ms. Nopnapha.

139
00:11:24,640 --> 00:11:27,320
- Ma'am, could we have an interview?
- Could we interview you, please?

140
00:11:27,500 --> 00:11:28,501
Just a quick interview, please.

141
00:11:28,688 --> 00:11:30,640
How are you feeling right now, ma'am?

142
00:11:30,902 --> 00:11:31,903
Well...

143
00:11:32,200 --> 00:11:35,560
Nothing's broken. Just a minor sprain.

144
00:11:38,064 --> 00:11:40,752
You're still working with a cast on?

145
00:11:41,065 --> 00:11:42,920
The work of the nation can't be put on hold.

146
00:11:43,066 --> 00:11:45,480
I'm made of steel. I can still work.

147
00:11:47,080 --> 00:11:49,840
Could you tell us how the incident happened, ma'am?

148
00:11:49,900 --> 00:11:52,080
How did you end up falling down the escalator?

149
00:11:53,990 --> 00:11:55,720
Well... It was an accident.

150
00:11:56,726 --> 00:11:58,992
I tripped over my high heels.

151
00:11:59,000 --> 00:12:01,720
And tumbled down. That's all there is to it.

152
00:12:02,939 --> 00:12:05,140
So someone happened to see you fall

153
00:12:05,200 --> 00:12:06,920
and pressed the emergency stop button, right?

154
00:12:08,400 --> 00:12:09,401
That's right.

155
00:12:09,700 --> 00:12:13,120
That young woman also works as a civil servant at this ministry.

156
00:12:13,800 --> 00:12:15,200
I owe her my thanks.

157
00:12:16,934 --> 00:12:19,880
And may I ask what happened to your face, ma'am?

158
00:12:20,870 --> 00:12:21,871
Uh...

159
00:12:23,300 --> 00:12:24,301
Well...

160
00:12:24,832 --> 00:12:26,200
I hit the handrail.

161
00:12:26,390 --> 00:12:27,920
I hit my face against the handrail right here.

162
00:12:28,347 --> 00:12:29,440
It really hurts.

163
00:12:32,027 --> 00:12:35,140
- You're bruised all over, aren't you?
- It must have hurt so much.

164
00:13:12,960 --> 00:13:13,961
What did you just throw away?

165
00:13:16,091 --> 00:13:17,960
A brick. Can't you see?

166
00:13:18,400 --> 00:13:20,512
What kind of normal person carries a brick around?

167
00:13:21,664 --> 00:13:23,500
I thought only car thieves did that.

168
00:13:24,589 --> 00:13:26,656
Didn't you know I have a side hustle?

169
00:13:28,080 --> 00:13:30,280
Seriously, why are you carrying a brick?

170
00:13:31,445 --> 00:13:32,446
To stop my car from rolling.

171
00:13:33,500 --> 00:13:34,640
Can I believe anything you say?

172
00:13:36,000 --> 00:13:37,301
Why are you interrogating me?

173
00:13:37,422 --> 00:13:40,320
I'm not your suspect, Mr. Alpaca.

174
00:13:41,051 --> 00:13:42,240
Can you stop calling me Alpaca?

175
00:13:42,726 --> 00:13:43,727
Call me Al Pacino.

176
00:13:45,419 --> 00:13:46,420
Just kidding.

177
00:13:48,731 --> 00:13:49,760
I wanted to ask you something.

178
00:13:52,072 --> 00:13:53,120
What happened yesterday?

179
00:13:54,430 --> 00:13:55,431
Do you even have to ask?

180
00:13:55,971 --> 00:13:58,172
Your aunt-in-law picked a fight with me, as usual.

181
00:13:58,707 --> 00:14:00,300
But the difference is,

182
00:14:01,935 --> 00:14:03,160
this time, I fought back.

183
00:14:03,998 --> 00:14:05,300
And I'm never backing down again.

184
00:14:36,800 --> 00:14:38,201
Are we discussing work or something else?

185
00:14:39,835 --> 00:14:41,920
If it's personal, let's talk about it at home.

186
00:14:44,755 --> 00:14:48,100
Then I'll use my authority to order you to discuss personal matters with me right here.

187
00:14:48,664 --> 00:14:50,640
Since we're hardly ever home at the same time.

188
00:15:10,563 --> 00:15:12,200
Do you know what happened last night?

189
00:15:14,248 --> 00:15:15,650
Exactly what you said in the interview.

190
00:15:16,584 --> 00:15:17,680
You tripped over your heels.

191
00:15:21,585 --> 00:15:25,880
She hit me in the face with a blunt object and sent me tumbling down the stairs.

192
00:15:27,091 --> 00:15:28,592
Not just once.

193
00:15:28,862 --> 00:15:30,360
- But three times!
- Hey!

194
00:15:31,342 --> 00:15:34,100
If you're going to accuse Mutta, at least make it believable.

195
00:15:34,390 --> 00:15:37,391
If she told me you attacked her, I'd believe that.

196
00:15:38,528 --> 00:15:39,880
Stop being such a fool!

197
00:15:40,715 --> 00:15:43,116
That bitch Mutta isn't as innocent as you think!

198
00:15:44,716 --> 00:15:46,840
What kind of shameless woman steals another woman's husband?

199
00:15:47,100 --> 00:15:48,801
How rotten must she be inside?

200
00:15:48,840 --> 00:15:52,320
I think you need to understand our relationship better.

201
00:15:53,170 --> 00:15:54,840
I don't love you anymore.

202
00:15:55,170 --> 00:15:57,100
So I don't belong to you.

203
00:15:57,814 --> 00:15:59,560
Mutta is the woman I love.

204
00:16:00,166 --> 00:16:01,920
I was the one who pursued her.

205
00:16:02,000 --> 00:16:03,801
She didn't steal me from you.

206
00:16:05,056 --> 00:16:06,700
She seduced you!

207
00:16:06,854 --> 00:16:08,220
That's why you fell for her!

208
00:16:10,307 --> 00:16:11,320
If she weren't in the picture,

209
00:16:11,500 --> 00:16:13,301
- Would you have stopped loving me?
- Yes!

210
00:16:14,067 --> 00:16:15,080
I would've stopped loving you anyway.

211
00:16:15,838 --> 00:16:17,960
Even if you were the last woman on Earth,

212
00:16:18,259 --> 00:16:19,860
I'd rather fall in love with a man.

213
00:16:20,414 --> 00:16:22,240
Hell, I'd rather sleep with a man!

214
00:16:23,115 --> 00:16:24,483
Stop blaming other people!

215
00:16:24,766 --> 00:16:27,440
The reason I stopped loving you is because of you.

216
00:16:27,500 --> 00:16:28,560
Not anyone else.

217
00:16:29,574 --> 00:16:31,075
You can't stop loving me!

218
00:16:31,318 --> 00:16:33,219
- Because we're husband and wife!
- Of course I can!

219
00:16:33,230 --> 00:16:35,400
Why can't I? I just don't love you anymore!

220
00:16:35,478 --> 00:16:37,640
Even if you killed me, I'd never love you again!

221
00:16:37,803 --> 00:16:38,804
You have to love me!

222
00:16:39,712 --> 00:16:40,960
Think carefully, Phop.

223
00:16:41,622 --> 00:16:42,880
Without me,

224
00:16:43,654 --> 00:16:45,250
you wouldn't be a director.

225
00:16:45,360 --> 00:16:47,361
You wouldn't get to sip wine and sign papers all day.

226
00:16:47,542 --> 00:16:49,840
Or take 200 days off a year and show up late.

227
00:16:51,120 --> 00:16:53,878
I could demote you to a janitor anytime I want!

228
00:16:55,030 --> 00:16:58,614
Go ahead! Do it! Think carefully, Nopnapha.

229
00:16:59,126 --> 00:17:01,360
The beloved female minister of the people.

230
00:17:01,392 --> 00:17:04,370
You think someone like you would accept having a janitor for a husband?

231
00:17:04,515 --> 00:17:06,440
I don't believe it! Go ahead!

232
00:17:06,547 --> 00:17:08,056
Do it! I'd love to be a janitor!

233
00:17:08,088 --> 00:17:09,089
Go ahead!

234
00:17:09,315 --> 00:17:12,240
Hey! Get me a mop! I want to be a janitor!

235
00:17:12,286 --> 00:17:14,387
Bring me a mop! Come on!

236
00:17:14,614 --> 00:17:15,615
Come back here right now!

237
00:17:26,768 --> 00:17:27,769
Phop!

238
00:17:29,440 --> 00:17:31,000
Calm down, ma'am. Please calm down.

239
00:17:31,339 --> 00:17:32,520
Keep it together, ma'am.

240
00:17:33,387 --> 00:17:34,388
Please calm down.

241
00:17:35,549 --> 00:17:36,550
Take a deep breath.

242
00:17:36,579 --> 00:17:37,700
Breathe in for four, out for six.

243
00:17:38,286 --> 00:17:41,480
Breathe in. One... two... three...

244
00:17:44,030 --> 00:17:47,120
Has Phop really gone this crazy over that woman?

245
00:17:48,696 --> 00:17:50,600
He already has a perfect family.

246
00:17:51,347 --> 00:17:53,600
A good wife and wonderful children.

247
00:17:55,416 --> 00:17:57,280
I'll never understand men.

248
00:17:59,417 --> 00:18:02,320
Then why haven't you fired that mistress yet, Mom?

249
00:18:02,814 --> 00:18:04,880
Isn't having an affair a serious disciplinary offense?

250
00:18:05,443 --> 00:18:06,445
If I did that,

251
00:18:06,776 --> 00:18:09,777
I'd be announcing to everyone that your father cheated on me.

252
00:18:13,100 --> 00:18:14,840
Then just frame her for something else.

253
00:18:15,112 --> 00:18:16,440
Theft, embezzlement, anything.

254
00:18:18,000 --> 00:18:19,801
We'd still have to set up an investigation committee.

255
00:18:20,131 --> 00:18:23,132
And Dad would chair it, so she'd get away with it anyway.

256
00:18:33,296 --> 00:18:34,790
If we can't fire her,

257
00:18:35,523 --> 00:18:38,360
we can make her life miserable until she quits.

258
00:18:38,840 --> 00:18:40,280
Oh, that's right!

259
00:18:40,510 --> 00:18:43,250
Oshi, you're so good at coming up with wicked ideas.

260
00:18:43,710 --> 00:18:44,979
We need to find ways to bully her.

261
00:18:45,288 --> 00:18:46,534
Make her so miserable she jumps off a building.

262
00:18:48,123 --> 00:18:49,124
No way.

263
00:18:49,584 --> 00:18:52,840
I just gave an interview about the Stop Bullying campaign in schools.

264
